**Migration behavior for legacy 'default' (src-tauri/src/ipc/project.rs)**  
- On first boot, if no project is registered for the current root, the backend auto-registers it under the derived workspaceId (derived from the repo root name, e.g. 'orca-lite').  
- Legacy 'default' is treated as a soft alias ➜  the frontend will receive the new id on the first successful `cmd_project_startup` call and can migrate localStorage/workspaceId accordingly.  
- Subsequent calls to `cmd_project_register("default", …)` will fail with `WorkspaceAlreadyRegistered` if the root is already owned by another id.

